{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"],["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"Design Principles","role":"article"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"},"sections":[],"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp"],"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"],"title":"Explanation","anchor":"Explanation"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux’s surface area looks small — a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol — but the API is opinionated. These principles explain "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"why"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the API has the shape it does, so you can extend it correctly."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"1-State-is-a-value-observation-is-a-class","type":"heading","text":"1. State is a value, observation is a class"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"State is a struct. Mutations go through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout State"},{"text":", which is predictable, snapshottable, and testable. SwiftUI observation needs an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" reference type. Reconciling these two requires a class that mirrors the struct.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" generates that class for you ("},{"code":"<StructName>Observer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") and wires up the "},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance that bridges the two. Don’t hand-write the observer. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"pack → reduce → unpack-diff → observe","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cycle is what gives you per-property re-renders without coupling reducers to a class.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"type":"text","text":" extends this to nested struct slices: each slice gets its own observer class so observation stays granular even across composition."}]},{"anchor":"2-Reducers-are-pure-and-synchronous","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"2. Reducers are pure and synchronous"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers take "},{"code":"inout State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and an "},{"code":"Action","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", mutate state in place, and return an optional "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". They never "},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", never "},{"code":"throw","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and never call I\/O directly."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why: pure synchronous mutations are trivially testable, deterministic, and snapshot-friendly. When you need async work (network, disk, timers), return an effect — a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" async closure that runs off the MainActor and dispatches follow-up actions back through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"3-Effects-run-off-MainActor-sends-hop-back","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"3. Effects run off MainActor; sends hop back"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable (Send) async -> Void"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":" runs effects in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task { @concurrent in }"},{"type":"text","text":" so they don’t block UI. "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor @Sendable (Action) -> Void"},{"type":"text","text":", so dispatching from inside an effect always lands back on MainActor — no manual hops, no race conditions on state."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The split is deliberate: effects own the work, the reducer owns the state.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"4. Persistence is invisible","anchor":"4-Persistence-is-invisible","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers mutate "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" properties; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" records every change in a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" debounces and drains those changesets through "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" closures."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You never write ","type":"text"},{"code":"db.save()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in a feature. A reducer that adds an item is identical whether the entity is persisted to SwiftData, SQLite, or nowhere — register or don’t register a writer. This is the principle that makes Swidux apps feel small: persistence stops being a concern of feature code.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"5. Synchronous state, async persistence","anchor":"5-Synchronous-state-async-persistence","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State updates synchronously inside the reducer for instant UI feedback. Persistence happens asynchronously: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"text":" change tracking is in-memory and free; the debounced persistence flush coalesces rapid mutations into a single batched write.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Tap-tap-tap-tap on an increment button updates the UI on every tap and produces one DB write a moment later. Reducers stay synchronous; storage stays cheap.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"6-Plugins-are-the-single-extension-point","level":2,"text":"6. Plugins are the single extension point","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Everything that hangs off the dispatch cycle is a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":". Persistence, undo, killswitch, parental gate, paywall — same protocol, same lifecycle hooks. You can add your own without forking Swidux.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Two structural patterns:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core middleware"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") — action-agnostic. Doesn’t know your action type. Couples only to state shape ("},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for undo; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" keypaths for persistence)."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Domain plugins"}]},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchPlugin"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParentalGatePlugin"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"text":", your own) — owns a state slice and an action enum. Wires into your root types via keypath + action lifter + extractor.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The decision rule: "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"does this need to know your action type?"}]},{"type":"text","text":" If no, write core middleware and use "},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". If yes, write a domain plugin and use "},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"7. Bind to the store, not to `@State`","anchor":"7-Bind-to-the-store-not-to-State"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Form inputs read from the store and dispatch on write. Use ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for the common case (read one property, dispatch one action), and fall back to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Binding(get:set:)"},{"text":" when the read is a transformation (optional unwraps, derived values) or the setter wraps the dispatch in animation or branching. Don’t buffer mutable form state in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":" and write back on a button.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why: every mutation flows through the reducer, which means undo\/redo, persistence, and any plugin that watches the dispatch cycle sees every keystroke (subject to coalescing). If you stash state in "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", those plugins are blind to it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The trade-off is more dispatches per keystroke. Coalescing — see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"text":" — collapses bursts of the same action into a single undo step.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"8. Registration order matters at the boundaries","anchor":"8-Registration-order-matters-at-the-boundaries"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" snapshots in "},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so it must run "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}]},{"type":"text","text":" any plugin or reducer mutates state — register it first. "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" drains changelogs in ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so it wants the post-mutation state — register it after undo. Domain plugins use only ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so their relative order rarely matters.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The recommended order:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. snapshots first","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. drains after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. domain plugins","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)","plugins.register(parentalGatePlugin)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"text":"9. Strict concurrency, on purpose","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"9-Strict-concurrency-on-purpose"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux is built for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swiftLanguageMode(.v6)"},{"type":"text","text":" and assumes Swift 6 strict concurrency throughout. State must be "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":". The macros mark generated code carefully. Effects use explicit isolation ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@concurrent"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This is friction at first — you’ll get warnings about ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"text":" types. Honour them. The result is a state-management layer that composes safely with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async\/await"},{"text":" and SwiftData without the surprise data races you get from pre-Swift 6 designs.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"10. The store is opinionated; your app is not","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"10-The-store-is-opinionated-your-app-is-not"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux gives you a "},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol, and three optional plugins. It does not give you:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A dependency-injection container (write your own "},{"code":"AppEnvironment","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A navigation library (use SwiftUI navigation)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A network layer (use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"text":", structured concurrency, or whatever you want).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An opinion on database (SwiftData, GRDB, SQLite, Core Data — register a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" and Swidux doesn’t care)."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The store owns one job: take an action, produce a new state, run effects. Everything else is yours."}]},{"text":"11. Service shapes: protocol when others implement it, closures when we own it","anchor":"11-Service-shapes-protocol-when-others-implement-it-closures-when-we-own-it","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux services deliberately come in two shapes, chosen by who supplies the implementation:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Protocol"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — when apps or vendor adapters implement the backend:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"PaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (RevenueCat, StoreKit, simulated), "},{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(Mixpanel, Amplitude, console), "},{"code":"FeatureFlagsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (any JSON host)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A protocol gives conformers a stable, documented contract."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Struct of closures"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — when the library owns the shape and apps only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"configure or mock it: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchService"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParentalChallengeSource"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SyncPreflightService"},{"type":"text","text":". Closures make the built-in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".live"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".mock"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"factories and per-test overrides trivial without a conformance ceremony."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The split is a signal, not an accident: if you find yourself conforming to a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"struct-of-closures service, that service was designed to be configured, not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"replaced."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Anti-patterns","anchor":"Anti-patterns"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"try"},{"type":"text","text":" inside a reducer — return an effect instead."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Hand-writing the observer class when you could use "},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Calling "},{"code":"db.save()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from inside a reducer — use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Mutating state from inside an effect — effects dispatch actions; the reducer mutates.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Owning the store with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@StateObject"},{"type":"text","text":" — use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":", not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ObservableObject"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Buffering form state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" and committing on submit — bind to the store directly."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Registering "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" before "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — snapshot must precede mutation."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","title":"Plugin Architecture"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Send":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/send","kind":"symbol","title":"Send","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A function for dispatching actions back to the store from within an effect."}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Send"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Send"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","title":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingYourFirstApp":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingyourfirstapp","kind":"article","title":"Build Your First Swidux App","abstract":[{"text":"Build a counter app from scratch and meet the four moving parts of a Swidux project: state, action, reducer, and store.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux","kind":"symbol","title":"Swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","role":"collection"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","kind":"symbol","title":"PersistencePlugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ChangeSet":{"title":"ChangeSet","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ChangeSet"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/changeset","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ChangeSet","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tracks which entity IDs have been created\/updated or deleted."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"type":"topic","title":"EntityStore","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"title":"UndoPlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/StateWriter":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Accumulates entity snapshots and produces batched async persistence work.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"StateWriter","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"StateWriter"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"StateWriter"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/statewriter"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"title":"Effect","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"An async unit of work returned by a reducer.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","title":"Architecture & Performance","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SecurityPosture":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What Swidux’s soft controls actually guarantee, and what to do when you need a hard one."}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/securityposture","title":"Security Posture"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/binding(_:sending:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/binding(_:sending:)","kind":"symbol","title":"binding(_:sending:)","abstract":[{"text":"Creates a SwiftUI ","type":"text"},{"code":"Binding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that reads a property through the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observer tree and dispatches an action when written.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"binding"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s7KeyPathC","text":"KeyPath"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"State"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux0A10ObservableP8ObserverQa","text":"Observer"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"sending"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI7BindingV","text":"Binding"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"role":"symbol"}}}